    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0609" n="597" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg597"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lieutenant General Alvan C.
                            Gillem, Jr., to Colonel J. Hart
                            Caughey at Yenan</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-24">24 March 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>359. Good work. General Chang agrees to 3-paragraph directive that he and General
                    Chou had prepared and discussed previously.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d267-f1"/>
                    General Chang also agrees to the inclusion of the words “and fair” in paragraph
                    3. Inform General Chou that I am presenting General Chang with the memorandum
                    reference Canton and Hankow.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d267-f2"/> Team has returned
                    to Hankow area.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d267-f1" n="43" xml:id="d267-f1-content">
                <p>See draft prepared by General Chou En-lai, <ref target="#pg564">p. 564</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d267-f2" n="44" xml:id="d267-f2-content">
                <p>March 24, <ref target="#pg617">p. 617</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
